.556491,"y":0.987038,"area":484},{"id":713,"colour":85,"x":0.12772,"y":0.990787,"area":409}],"source":{"title":"Laced moray ( Gymnothorax favagineus ), Ad Dimaniyat Islands, Oman. This moray, also called leopard moray eel, can reach a maximum length of 3 metres (9.8 ft). The laced moray lives on the outer slopes of coral reefs and is widespread throughout the Indo-West Pacific area from eastern coast of Africa, Red Sea included, to Papua New Guinea and from southern Japan to the Great Barrier Reef.","creator":"Diego Delso","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","pageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/?curid=151812091","provider":"Wikimedia Commons"}}